  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply the numerator and the denominator of the fraction by $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1.$ This gives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x-1} & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x-1}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1}{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1)}{{csc}^{2}\u2061x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity ${csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1={cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1)}{{csc}^{2}\u2061x-1}-1 & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1)}{{cot}^{2}\u2061x}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}\u2061x}\\,(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1)}{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}\u2061x}}-1 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+1)\\,-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
